{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "pioneer-ddj-sb",
  "name": "DDJ-SB",
  "vendor": "Pioneer DJ",
  "ports": [
    "DDJ-SB"
  ],
  "evidence": "DDJ-SB captured with midi_probe on Windows 11 (WinMM, 2026-11-17) and macOS (CoreMIDI, 2026-11-22). Verified addresses were observed in hardware captures. Unverified addresses were inferred or transcribed and still need confirmation.",
  "notes": [
    "Faders, knobs, EQ and filters are 14-bit: CC n carries the high 7 bits and CC n + 0x20 the low 7.",
    "Buttons send Note On 0x7F when pressed and Note On 0x00 when released.",
    "Jogs send offset-64 steps. Touching the top sends note 0x35; turning it sends CC 0x23, the side CC 0x21.",
    "Both tempo faders on the unit tested move by themselves (steps of 48 to 64 out of 16383, about once a second), hence the dead band.",
    "SHIFT is handled by the controller: pads send other notes while it is held.",
    "Browse rotation is CC 0x40. Pressing Browse on the Mac sent note 0x41 on channel 7. The Windows capture also recorded 0x65 in the center section; its gesture needs to be checked again.",
    "The full CoreMIDI session also reported channel 2 note 0x47 without an identified gesture.",
    "Master and headphone level are analog, on the audio interface, and send no MIDI.",
    "The FX buttons are numbered here by unit and position."
  ],
